    {/* SECTION 08: THE LIMITS */}
    <SectionHeader num="08" title="The limits, applied to itself" />
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] md:text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 font-sans mb-12">
      <p>
        It is hindsight by construction. No organ sees a failure whose discovery is its first occurrence; the method makes the second instance cheap, and the first is always paid in full. Measurement can outgrow the product, and a machine that spends more on self-knowledge than on its work is a museum with good lighting. It cannot manufacture witnesses: a self-graded record performs to an empty room until distribution arrives. And it cannot act for the operator; the largest number in the record is often his own zero, and the method's only power over it is to refuse to lie about it.
      </p>
